> > On Friday, May 10, 2013 4:14:28 PM UTC+2, Robersy Sanchez wrote:
> > > Hi, Altuna
> > >
> > > Thank you very much for your answer.
> > >
> > > I have detected that the missing NAs are found in the "methylBase" object before apply function "tileMethylCounts". In particular, in the column numCs, which contains the counts for each CpG. Hence, it seems to be that function tileMethylCounts is not dealing well with missing data.
> > >
> > > These data were previously processed with BSMAP and then the methylation values were extracted with methratio.py. I wonder if the methylKit function read.bismark is able to read a sam file produced by BSMAP.
> > >
