I understand and it is OK, that's why I suggested you get some basic R fundamentals before you dwell in to this package.

You shouldn't provide the methylation file for read.transcript.features(), please follow the example.
what you need to do is just copy paste the code I sent earlier and read help for the read.transcript.features() function and see the example there. You just need to provide a bed file and some other optional arguments for that function to work.

 Unfortunately, I don't have time to walk you through every detail, that's why there is a documentation for each function and the vignette, and plenty of tutorials.

